WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.725 --> 00:00:03.101
What is that?

00:00:03.977 --> 00:00:04.853
Uh...

00:00:07.022 --> 00:00:10.484
It-- It's the speech Hop wrote
for you and Mike.

00:00:11.026 --> 00:00:11.985
Speech?

00:00:12.402 --> 00:00:14.613
Yeah. You know, the heart-to-heart.

00:00:17.783 --> 00:00:19.743
He never talked to you, did he?

00:00:21.661 --> 00:00:22.704
[scoffs]

00:00:25.457 --> 00:00:26.666
Can I read?

00:00:38.762 --> 00:00:41.973
[Hopper] "There's something I've been
wanting to talk to you both about.

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:45.811
I know this is a difficult conversation,

00:00:45.894 --> 00:00:48.647
but I care about you both very much.

00:00:49.356 --> 00:00:51.858
And I know that you care about each other
very much.

00:00:51.942 --> 00:00:55.612
And that's why it's important that
we set these boundaries moving forward,

00:00:55.695 --> 00:00:57.781
so we can build an environment...

00:01:01.326 --> 00:01:03.286
where we all feel...

00:01:04.913 --> 00:01:06.289
comfortable...

00:01:07.999 --> 00:01:09.167
trusted...

00:01:10.794 --> 00:01:12.003
and open...

00:01:14.506 --> 00:01:16.591
to sharing our feelings."

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:23.056
Feelings.

00:01:29.146 --> 00:01:30.147
[murmurs]

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:36.236
[Hopper] Feelings.

00:01:37.904 --> 00:01:39.072
Jesus.

00:01:39.281 --> 00:01:40.157
[chuckles]

00:01:40.657 --> 00:01:42.033
The truth is,

00:01:43.368 --> 00:01:46.830
for so long,
I'd forgotten what those even were.

00:01:48.415 --> 00:01:50.417
I've been stuck in one place,

00:01:50.959 --> 00:01:52.627
in a cave, you might say.

00:01:53.253 --> 00:01:54.880
A deep, dark cave.

00:01:55.881 --> 00:01:58.925
And then,
I left some Eggos out in the woods,

00:01:59.009 --> 00:02:01.094
and you came into my life and...

00:02:01.887 --> 00:02:05.015
for the first time in a long time,

00:02:07.309 --> 00:02:09.478
I started to feel things again.

00:02:10.604 --> 00:02:12.522
I started to feel happy.

00:02:16.735 --> 00:02:19.696
But, lately, I guess I've been feeling...

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:22.824
distant from you.

00:02:24.201 --> 00:02:25.243
Like you're...

00:02:26.453 --> 00:02:28.538
you're pulling away from me or something.

00:02:29.581 --> 00:02:31.833
I miss playing board games every night,

00:02:33.543 --> 00:02:37.506
making triple-decker Eggo extravaganzas
at sunrise,

00:02:38.089 --> 00:02:40.800
watching westerns together
before we doze off.

00:02:42.594 --> 00:02:44.221
But I know you're getting older.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:46.848
Growing.

00:02:47.641 --> 00:02:48.767
Changing.

00:02:50.393 --> 00:02:51.603
And I guess...

00:02:52.896 --> 00:02:54.356
if I'm being really honest,

00:02:55.357 --> 00:02:56.733
that's what scares me.

00:02:58.902 --> 00:03:00.779
I don't want things to change.

00:03:04.950 --> 00:03:07.244
So, I think maybe that's why
I came in here,

00:03:07.327 --> 00:03:10.497
to try to maybe... stop that change.

00:03:12.332 --> 00:03:13.917
To turn back the clock.

00:03:14.918 --> 00:03:18.088
To make things go back
to how they were.

00:03:19.381 --> 00:03:21.675
[Hopper sighs deeply]

00:03:23.009 --> 00:03:24.594
But I know that's naive.

00:03:25.554 --> 00:03:26.471
It's just...

00:03:27.681 --> 00:03:29.099
not how life works.

00:03:29.933 --> 00:03:31.184
It's moving.

00:03:31.977 --> 00:03:34.479
Always moving, whether you like it or not.

00:03:36.398 --> 00:03:39.651
And, yeah, sometimes it's painful.

00:03:40.944 --> 00:03:42.279
Sometimes it's sad.

00:03:43.822 --> 00:03:45.323
And sometimes...

00:03:46.449 --> 00:03:47.867
it's surprising.

00:03:49.369 --> 00:03:50.328
Happy.

00:03:52.747 --> 00:03:53.832
So, you know what?

00:03:54.958 --> 00:03:56.167
Keep on growing up, kid.

00:03:57.335 --> 00:03:58.878
Don't let me stop you.

00:03:59.838 --> 00:04:02.465
Make mistakes, learn from 'em,

00:04:03.383 --> 00:04:06.386
and when life hurts you,
because it will,

00:04:07.387 --> 00:04:08.805
remember the hurt.

00:04:09.806 --> 00:04:12.517
The hurt is good.

00:04:13.226 --> 00:04:15.645
It means you're out of that cave.

00:04:17.981 --> 00:04:19.566
But, please,

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.027
if you don't mind,

00:04:22.986 --> 00:04:25.530
for the sake of your poor old dad,

00:04:26.364 --> 00:04:30.285
keep the door open three inches.

00:04:30.368 --> 00:04:31.411
[laughs]

00:04:33.288 --> 00:04:34.456
[sniffles]

00:04:36.082 --> 00:04:36.916
[sobs]

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.002
["Heroes" by Peter Gabriel playing]

00:04:39.336 --> 00:04:41.087
♪ I ♪

00:04:43.548 --> 00:04:45.133
♪ I will be king... ♪

00:04:46.176 --> 00:04:47.427
[knocking on door]

00:04:49.387 --> 00:04:50.764
Are you okay?

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:55.185
Yeah.

00:04:57.729 --> 00:04:58.772
[sniffles]

00:04:59.272 --> 00:05:00.482
Time to go?

00:05:02.025 --> 00:05:03.109
Yeah.

00:05:04.027 --> 00:05:05.820
I'll be out in a minute.

00:05:07.155 --> 00:05:08.239
Okay.

00:05:09.574 --> 00:05:11.701
♪ Oh, we could be heroes ♪

00:05:15.413 --> 00:05:17.165
♪ Just for one day ♪

00:05:20.251 --> 00:05:22.253
♪ Oh, we can be us ♪

00:05:25.674 --> 00:05:27.842
♪ Just for one day ♪

